### Food Delivery Platform - Delivery Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Prerequisites: run user-service.http ... order-service.http first, so the customer has an address and the
### owner below has an ACTIVE restaurant (in Bengaluru) with menu items, open now.
###
### How a delivery happens:
###   the restaurant marks the order READY_FOR_PICKUP -> a delivery is created (PENDING)
###   -> the assignment job (every 5s) offers it to the AVAILABLE partner in the restaurant's city who has waited
###      longest (ASSIGNED) -> the partner accepts within 2 minutes (ACCEPTED), or it goes to the next partner
###   -> pickup (PICKED_UP: the order becomes OUT_FOR_DELIVERY) -> delivered (DELIVERED: the order too).
###
### Caller identity: the access token of a sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer); its role must be
###   DELIVERY_PARTNER for /delivery/partners and /delivery/deliveries, CUSTOMER for
###   /delivery/orders (tracking), PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**

@gateway = http://localhost:8080

@partnerEmail = ravi.rider@example.com
@partnerPassword = Rider1234
@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@ownerEmail = arjun.spicehub@example.com
@ownerPassword = Owner1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

# Change for every new order (one key per checkout)
@checkoutKey = delivery-demo-0001

@partnerId = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@addressId = {{addresses.response.body.$[0].id}}
@restaurantId = {{myRestaurants.response.body.$[0].id}}
@firstItemId = {{menu.response.body.$.sections[0].items[0].id}}
@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}
@deliveryId = {{current.response.body.$.id}}


### ============================ SETUP ============================

### 1. Register a delivery partner (409 if it already exists: fine). UserRegistered creates the partner in
###    delivery-partner-service, whose DeliveryPartnerChanged event adds them to delivery-service's dispatch list.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{partnerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{partnerPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Ravi Kumar",
  "phone": "+919900112233",
  "role": "DELIVERY_PARTNER"
}

### 2. Logins -> partnerId, customerToken, ownerToken, adminToken
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{partnerEmail}}", "password": "{{partnerPassword}}" }

###
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}" }

###
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{ownerPassword}}" }

###
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### ===================== PARTNER: PROFILE AND AVAILABILITY =====================

### 3. My partner profile (OFFLINE, readyToWork false until vehicle and city are set) - delivery-partner-service
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 4. Going online without a vehicle: 422
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "AVAILABLE" }

### 5. Vehicle and city (deliveries are offered from restaurants in this city) - delivery-partner-service
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleType": "MOTORCYCLE", "vehicleNumber": "KA01AB1234", "city": "Bengaluru" }

### 6. Go online
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "AVAILABLE" }


### ================= AN ORDER TO DELIVER (cash on delivery) =================

### 7. The customer's address -> addressId
# @name addresses
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 8. The owner's restaurant and its menu -> restaurantId, firstItemId
# @name myRestaurants
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
# @name menu
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu

### 9. Cart and checkout -> orderId
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/cart/items/{{firstItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 1 }

###
# @name placeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{checkoutKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "addressId": {{addressId}}, "paymentMethod": "CASH_ON_DELIVERY" }

### 10. The restaurant accepts, prepares and marks it ready (run all three)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/preparing
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ready
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ========================= PARTNER: THE DELIVERY =========================

### 11. Within a few seconds the delivery is offered to me -> deliveryId (204 if not yet: try again)
###     I also get a push notification: GET /api/v1/notifications as the partner
# @name current
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/current
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 12a. Accept (within 2 minutes, otherwise the offer goes to someone else and I go OFFLINE)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 12b. ... or decline (instead of 12a): it is offered to the next partner, never to me again
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Flat tyre" }

### 13. The customer sees who brings the food (and can call them while they are on the way)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 13a. My phone's position while on the way (the partner page sends it by itself): 204. Sent again within 2 s it
###      is skipped; 409 before accepting or after delivering. Only the latest position is kept.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/location
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latitude": 12.9716, "longitude": 77.5946, "accuracyMeters": 12, "headingDeg": 90 }

### 13b. The customer's live map: the partner's last position, the restaurant and the drop-off (404 until accepted)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/orders/{{orderId}}/live
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 14. Picked up at the restaurant (the order becomes OUT_FOR_DELIVERY)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### 15. Delivered without confirming the cash: 422 (cash on delivery)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 16. Delivered, cash collected: put the order total (cashToCollect from step 11)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine/{{deliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cashCollected": {{current.response.body.$.cashToCollect}} }

### 17. The order is DELIVERED and PAID (order-service applied DeliveryStatusChanged)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 18. My history and my profile (AVAILABLE again, completedDeliveries + 1)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/mine?status=DELIVERED
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/delivery/partners/me
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### ===================== ADMIN: DELIVERY PARTNERS =====================
### Through the gateway: search, one partner, deactivate, activate and audit trail are delivery-partner-service;
### availability, stats and a partner's deliveries are delivery-service (see delivery-partner-service.http).

### 19. Partners in a city, by status
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners?city=Bengaluru&status=AVAILABLE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 20. How many are available, busy, offline, suspended right now
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 21. One partner and their deliveries
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/deliveries
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 22. Deactivate (suspend) - 409 while the partner is on a delivery (reassign it first)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Documents expired" }

### 23. Activate again (the partner starts OFFLINE and goes online themselves)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "New documents verified" }

### 24. The partner's audit trail
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{partnerId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================== ADMIN: DELIVERIES ========================

### 25. Search (filters: status, orderId, partnerUserId, customerId, restaurantId, city, fromDate, toDate)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries?city=Bengaluru&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26. Delayed deliveries: no partner 10 min after the food was ready, or not delivered after 45 min
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/delayed
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 27. Today's report: per status, average delivery time, delayed now
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 28. One delivery with its full timeline (offers, declines, timeouts, reassignments)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 29. Reassign a delivery that is not picked up yet (audited): to an AVAILABLE partner ...
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/reassign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partnerUserId": {{partnerId}}, "reason": "Partner is next to the restaurant" }

### 30. ... or back to the queue (the assignment job finds someone else)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/reassign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Partner not answering the phone" }

### 31. The delivery's audit trail
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka, Phase 10) =======================
### delivery-service writes DeliveryStatusChanged to its transactional outbox (key = orderId) on every step:
###   order-service       PICKED_UP -> order OUT_FOR_DELIVERY, DELIVERED -> order DELIVERED (+ PAID for cash)
###   notification-service ASSIGNED -> push to the partner, ACCEPTED -> push to the customer (partner, vehicle),
###                        CANCELLED -> push to the partner who was on it
### It also writes DeliveryPartnerStatusChanged (key = partnerUserId) whenever a partner's status changes.
### It consumes: DeliveryPartnerChanged (partners), RestaurantChanged (pickup addresses), OrderCreated (customer and
### drop-off), OrderStatusChanged READY_FOR_PICKUP (starts the delivery), OrderCancelled (cancels it).
### Details whose events never arrived are fetched from order-service / restaurant-service by the assignment job.
### Messages: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.delivery.status-changed-value/versions/latest


### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health (direct)
GET http://localhost:8087/actuator/health

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8087/swagger-ui.html
GET http://localhost:8087/v3/api-docs
